            <div xml:id="d475-a2">

                <pb facs="0502" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 2.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Gorogio to Mr.
                        Pruyn</head>
                <p>We have to inform you that, in accordance with our instructions, Sibata Sadataro
                    agreed with you upon a reduction of duties.</p>
                <p>We will also reduce the duties on other import articles as per accompanying
                    statement, to take effect at the time agreed upon with you.</p>
                <p>Having notified the governors of the opened ports accordingly, we request you to
                    make this also known to your consuls at those ports.</p>
                <p>With respect and courtesy.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian japanese-nengō"
                            when="1864-02-04">The 29th day of the 12th month of the 3d year of
                            Bunkiu, (February 4, 1864</date>.)</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>ITAKURA SUWO-NO-KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>INOWUYE KAWATSI-NO-KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of America,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d475-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d475-a2-a1"/>
